init installs the skill stub for the agents you pick. With --project it installs into the project and points AGENTS.md at
the skill. A second run changes nothing.

```console
$ stetdoc init --project --agent codex,cursor,cmx2 --dry-run
note: no author is saved, and every revision needs one. Run stetdoc init --author "Your Name", or set STETDOC_AUTHOR, before you edit.
would write .agents/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (Codex, Cursor)
would write .cmx2/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (cmx2)
would write AGENTS.md

$ stetdoc init --project --agent codex,cursor,cmx2
note: no author is saved, and every revision needs one. Run stetdoc init --author "Your Name", or set STETDOC_AUTHOR, before you edit.
wrote .agents/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (Codex, Cursor)
wrote .cmx2/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (cmx2)
wrote AGENTS.md

$ stetdoc init --project --agent codex,cursor,cmx2
note: no author is saved, and every revision needs one. Run stetdoc init --author "Your Name", or set STETDOC_AUTHOR, before you edit.
unchanged .agents/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (Codex, Cursor)
unchanged .cmx2/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (cmx2)
unchanged AGENTS.md

$ stetdoc init --project --agent claude-code --mcp
note: Claude Code can also block other ways into a .docx, such as unzip or python-docx, with the guard hook the stetdoc plugin carries. To add it to this install, see https://github.com/clauseo-ai/stetdoc/blob/main/docs/agents.md#the-claude-code-guard-hook
note: no author is saved, and every revision needs one. Run stetdoc init --author "Your Name", or set STETDOC_AUTHOR, before you edit.
wrote .claude/skills/stetdoc/SKILL.md (Claude Code)
unchanged AGENTS.md

To use stetdoc as an MCP server as well, keep the skill installed with it: without the skill, an agent whose MCP server fails to start may edit the .docx's XML itself.
Register `stetdoc mcp` with each agent (init edits no agent's config):
  Claude Code: claude mcp add --scope project stetdoc -- stetdoc mcp

$ stetdoc init --project --remove --agent cursor
removed .agents/skills/stetdoc

$ stetdoc init --project --remove
removed .claude/skills/stetdoc
removed .cmx2/skills/stetdoc
removed the stetdoc block from AGENTS.md

$ stetdoc init --agent nobody
? 2
error[invalid_payload]: nobody is not an agent stetdoc installs for.
next: Name one or more of: claude-code, codex, cursor, opencode, openclaw, gemini, copilot, amp, hermes, grok, cmx2, factory, or all.

```
